Z||000014||sqoach||09-06-2001||11:41 AM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by pontiacs4me:<BR>[B]Im selling my last pair of paragon hood vents for $40 shipped, check them out!<P>Oh yeah. Those don't look too bad. Are they just bolt on? Or can I 'glass them in? Are they ready to paint?||||reg||1
Z||000015||pontiacs4me||09-07-2001||03:07 AM||||They are made of gelcoated fiberglass.  They need to be glassed in to look the best.  What I do is glue the vent down with some liquid nails, then sand the edge of the vent and on the hood next to it, then take some short strand fiberglass filler, mix up a little bit, and take your finger and spread a nice rounded bead into the corner.  Then take some 120 sand paper sand it all out smooth, then use some 220.  Then primer the whole area.  I just finished glassing mine in, and I did a pair of vents on my friends supercharged lumina.  They both look really nice.  Let me know if your interested.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Fiero5||09-07-2001||10:05 AM||||Phils da man.<BR>Can't waite to see his Lambo<BR>he says it's alot of work <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif</A> <P>Steve||||reg||12
Z||000017||sqoach||09-07-2001||06:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pontiacs4me:<BR><B>They are made of gelcoated fiberglass.  They need to be glassed in to look the best.  What I do is glue the vent down with some liquid nails, then sand the edge of the vent and on the hood next to it, then take some short strand fiberglass filler, mix up a little bit, and take your finger and spread a nice rounded bead into the corner.  Then take some 120 sand paper sand it all out smooth, then use some 220.  Then primer the whole area.  I just finished glassing mine in, and I did a pair of vents on my friends supercharged lumina.  They both look really nice.  Let me know if your interested.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'd like to buy them, but don't need them yet. It'll be a while before I paint my car and do any exterior work/mods. So I'm trying to save my money for getting it running nicely, re-doing some of the suspension, fixing the brakes, etc.||||reg||1
Z||000018||pontiacs4me||09-07-2001||09:53 PM||||sqoach,<P>Ok, the pair I have now are the last set from my first pair of molds.  The quality is ok, they need some primer work and sanding.  One of these days Im going to remake my molds, and the quality will be much better.  they will sell for $70+shipping.||||reg||1
